 3. ⚡ Exclusive: AI is hitting an energy wall 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Lindsey Bailey/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Silicon Valley moves fast and breaks things, but the U.S. electrical grid moves slowly and requires permits, Axios AI+ co-author Madison Mills writes. 

 The explosive growth of AI is colliding with the glacial pace of building out new power infrastructure, prompting a new warning from Goldman Sachs that energy bottlenecks are set to stall the AI race. Why it matters: Amid a wave of anxiety from Wall Street about the debt-fueled AI buildout, Goldman points to power as the biggest risk to trillions in spending in a new report shared exclusively with Axios.

 🔬 Zoom in: The U.S. has roughly 2,600 gigawatts of proposed power generation and storage projects awaiting grid connections, more than twice the grid's existing installed capacity, though many projects may never materialize.

 The median time from an application for a grid connection to commercial operation is roughly five years. 💰 Follow the money: The massive AI expansion is being financed with debt, raising the stakes if construction timelines slip.

 Goldman projects AI tech giants will borrow $420 billion globally in 2027, up more than 60% from its 2026 estimate. Keep reading . 

 
 
