 4. 💸 Charted: America&#x27;s expensive deficit 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Office of Management and Budget via FRED, U.S. Treasury. (2026 GDP estimated using extrapolated Q3 growth.) Chart: Emily Peck/Axios The U.S. budget deficit is ballooning and reached $2 trillion this fiscal year, Axios' Emily Peck writes. 

 Why it matters: That's the largest deficit since 2021, when the U.S. was climbing out of the pandemic recession. The deficit is driven in part by the cost of paying interest on the nation's enormous debt at a time when rates are rising.

 The federal government paid out $1.052 trillion in net interest on its outstanding debt for the 2026 fiscal year, which ended Sept. 30. Share this story ... Get Axios Markets . 

 
 
