 6. 🗳️ Stat du jour 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump points to a report by CNN's Harry Enten on a poll from May, shown during a rally last night in Park City, Kansas. Photo: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters Less than $1 of every $100 in Republican television ad spending on House and Senate races from Sept. 9 through Oct. 17 has gone toward commercials that mention the word "Trump," according to a New York Times analysis of broadcast and streaming ad data and transcripts from the media tracking firm AdImpact.

 💡 Axios' Alex Isenstadt tells me: Republicans say there's a simple reason President Trump's name isn't coming up in ads: He's just not popular.

 The party's internal numbers show him underwater in districts he won by as much as 15 points — meaning that for even candidates running in Trump country, it's better to talk about other things. Keep reading (NYT gift link). 
 
