 7. 🚀 Martian moon mystery 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A rendering of Japan's MMX probe reaching Mars' moon Phobos. Image: JAXA Japan has launched a potentially historic mission to scoop up soil samples from Phobos — one of Mars' two lumpy, potato-esque moons — and return them to Earth, Axios' Alex Fitzpatrick writes. 

 Why it matters: The Martian Moons eXploration (MMX) mission could reveal how the red planet's two weird little moons came to exist. 🌔 Some researchers believe they're remnants of a long-ago collision between Mars and some other body. Others think they're former asteroids captured by Mars' gravitational pull.

 Keep reading . 
 
