 8. ⚾ 1 for the road: Title-less World Series 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Tampa Bay Rays third baseman Junior Caminero slides into home past Cleveland Guardians catcher Patrick Bailey in Game 6 of the ALCS last night in St. Petersburg, Fla. Photo: David J. Phillip/AP The Tampa Bay Rays will face the Milwaukee Brewers in a World Series guaranteed to crown a first-time champion.

 The Rays beat the Cleveland Guardians in six games for the AL pennant. It'll be the first World Series between title-less teams since the Philadelphia Phillies defeated the Kansas City Royals in 1980.

 Milwaukee is MLB's smallest market . 🎲 The Brew Crew is favored to win the Fall Classic, which begins Friday night in Milwaukee.

